{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01WE8WB1TPXQpee9Nr16GkCy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Anchor is a single-user productivity + R&D mission-control system. Here's what it is, grounded in the project docs:\n\n- **Purpose:** A personal productivity system for J.C. Liechty that doubles as a \"mission control\" for AI-trio-driven R&D. It lives in one folder (`C:\\dev\\Anchor`), is plain-text/markdown-backed (no database, no syncing), and is meant to be a *truthful, useful memory* of each project's work.\n\n- **What it ships (the deliverable):** `anchor_gui.py` â€” a self-contained Python stdlib HTTP server that generates a browser dashboard at `http://localhost:8777`. It reads and writes the markdown files directly, runs persistently as the Windows NSSM service `anchor`, and has no external dependencies (one declared exception: optional `pywinpty` for the v3 terminal subsystem).\n\n- **Core productivity surface:** A task/project manager over markdown files (`DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, `domains/*.md`, etc.) with a full task lifecycle â€” active â†’ done â†’ cancelled â†’ saved-for-later â†’ restored â€” driven either through the interactive web GUI or a mirrored CLI (`anchor.py`).\n\n- **R&D control surface (v2 â†’ v3 \"Mission Control\"):** Turns each project into a cockpit for the trio **researchPrime (research) â†’ Crucible (planning) â†’ Foreman (build)**. It models trio runs as **sessions**, generates **cached, grounded summaries** of them, tracks effort history and \"grass-catcher\" ideas, and pins/runs **deliverables**. v3 adds real **ConPTY terminals** (xterm.js over a hand-rolled WebSocket), **per-session git-worktree isolation**, a stacking window manager, in-place expandable summaries, stage handoffs, an ephemeral deliverable **preview** server (hard-guarded off port 8777), and Ghost World Labs branding.\n\n- **Reliability/self-test:** A daily 5 AM health check (`anchor_healthcheck.py`) verifies file integrity, boots a throwaway server, exercises every endpoint and the full v2 **and** v3 R&D surfaces â€” all model calls stubbed (`ANCHOR_RUNNER_CMD` â†’ `fake_claude.py`, `ANCHOR_PTY_BACKEND=stub`), never touching live data or the `:8777` service.\n\n- **Current state (per memory/git):** v3 was built (all 10 waves green, 529 tests) and merged to master on 2026-06-12; the active branch `foreman/rnd-surface-v4` holds an in-progress **v4 redesign** (new branding mockups, project-window paradigms, and a proven ConPTYÃ—WebSocketÃ—xterm terminal harness) awaiting a paradigm decision before its Crucible/build.\n\nWant me to verify any of these against the actual code rather than the docs?"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4253,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":41003,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ab6b9371-0ad4-4064-ae01-c5e9a5aecbb5","uuid":"d9f7c308-d585-450b-af9e-12c2416da302","request_id":"req_011Cbyk8q9bdYWTMy9Xr7e84"}
